> How do I write "same" on a form that asks for two addresses, in German?
**assistant**:
> In German, if you want to indicate that two addresses are the same on a form, you can write "gleich" next to the second address field. This conveys that the information is identical. If you need to be more explicit, you could write "gleich wie oben" which means "same as above."
